# Marrow Journal — Signed-In App Architecture

Status: draft plan, written 2026-10-19 while the owner was away. Nothing here is built yet.
`docs/brief.md` wins over this document. If they disagree, fix this document.

Calls the brief did not settle are marked **[Assumed]** inline and collected in
[Assumptions](#assumptions) and [Open questions](#open-questions-for-the-owner) at the end.

---

## 1. Shape of the product

| Surface | Folder | Host | Rendering | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Public site | `apps/site` | `marrowjournal.com` **[Assumed domain]** | Next.js, static/server | Landing, pricing, `/privacy`, `/terms` |
| Signed-in app | `apps/app` | `app.marrowjournal.com` | Vite SPA, client-rendered behind auth | Today, calendar, entry, search, settings |
| Backend | `packages/backend` | Convex deployment | — | Schema, queries, mutations, jobs, webhooks |
| Domain rules | `packages/domain` | — | — | Route builders, query-state parsing, ID helper, plan rules, origins |

Staging: `preview.marrowjournal.com` and `preview.app.marrowjournal.com`. Local: site on `3000`, app on `3001`.

The site is in scope only because the app needs it. Google's OAuth consent screen will not verify without a
public home page and privacy policy, and Stripe expects terms.

Stack defaults: Clerk (auth), Convex (data and live sync), Stripe (billing), BlockNote (entry body), Vercel (hosting).
In code, modules are named by role (`auth`, `billing`, `search`), never by vendor.

---

## 2. Tenancy decision: one person, no workspaces

The brief says: **no sharing, no teams, no collaborators, now or later.** That changes the usual default.

- **No workspace or organization layer.** Clerk Organizations stay **disabled**. Clerk's personal-account mode is the
  only mode. Normally we would add a workspace boundary early "in case teams arrive." The owner has ruled teams out
  as positioning, so that boundary would only be one more thing that could leak.
- **The user is the only principal and the only owner.** Every private row belongs directly to one `users` row.
- **No tenancy segment in URLs.** Private routes have no `/w/[workspaceId]/…` prefix (see §5).
- **No sharing machinery of any kind.** No ACL tables, no share links, no public entry URLs, no "invite" email flows.
  If a future change proposes any of these, it contradicts the brief and has to go back to the owner.

If the owner ever reverses this, retrofitting a workspace layer costs a lot. That cost is accepted on purpose.

